# Requirements discovery

[I-001]: How should navigation work within the access model? #issue {"status":"open","parent":null}

[I-010]: What defines primary navigation? #issue {"status":"resolved","parent":"I-001","resolved_by":"D-007","resolution_history":["D-006","D-007"]}

[P-010A]: Workspaces define the root navigation hierarchy\. #position {"status":"rejected","issue":"I-010"}

[P-010B]: Operational areas define navigation\; a workspace is a context switcher\. #position {"status":"accepted","issue":"I-010"}

[E-021]: Users perform workflows that span workspaces\. #evidence {"status":"verified","issue":"I-010","handoff":"existing","sources":[{"kind":"user","ref":"Fixture scenario: daily cross-workspace work","authority":"intent"}]}

[C-008]: Navigation must stay usable with thirty workspaces\. #constraint {"status":"agreed","handoff":"invariant","sources":[{"kind":"user","ref":"Fixture scale envelope","authority":"intent"}]}

[C-012]: Navigation must never imply access to workspaces the user is not assigned to\. #constraint {"status":"verified","handoff":"invariant","sources":[{"kind":"spec","ref":"specs/access.md","authority":"normative","locator":"Access contract","sha256":"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"}]}

[E-031]: A thirty\-item workspace list needs scrolling on every visit\. #evidence {"status":"verified","sources":[{"kind":"research","ref":"https://example.com/usability-probe","authority":"observed","accessed":"2026-10-05"}]}

[I-030]: Would workspace roots stay usable at thirty workspaces? #issue {"status":"resolved","parent":"I-010","resolved_by":"E-031","resolution_history":["E-031"]}

[D-006]: Use operations\-first navigation\. #decision {"status":"superseded","superseded_by":"D-007","resolves":["I-010"],"selected":["P-010B"],"basis":"user","based_on":["E-021"],"rationale":"First agreement.","sources":[{"kind":"user","ref":"Fixture first agreement","authority":"intent"}]}

[D-007]: Use operations\-first navigation with a persistent workspace switcher in the header\. #decision {"status":"accepted","supersedes":"D-006","resolves":["I-010"],"selected":["P-010B"],"alternatives":["P-010A"],"basis":"user","based_on":["E-021","C-008","C-012","A-004"],"reaffirmed_by":["V-001","V-002"],"rationale":"Supports cross-workspace work at the stated scale.","sources":[{"kind":"user","ref":"Fixture agreement: \"switcher in the header\"","authority":"intent"}],"consequences":["The header shows the <workspace> context.","- a line that starts like a list item"],"terms":{"switcher":"The workspace selector in the header"},"rejection_reasons":{"P-010A":"Too many clicks."}}

[V-001]: The choice survives the first scope change\. #review {"status":"confirmed","decision":"D-007","based_on":["E-021"],"rationale":"Still valid after the first change."}

[V-002]: The choice still follows the current scope\. #review {"status":"confirmed","decision":"D-007","based_on":["C-008","C-012"],"rationale":"The current contracts suffice."}

[Q-000]: An older implication of the first agreement\. #consequence {"status":"superseded","derives_from":"D-006"}

[Q-001]: Cross\-workspace work needs a visible scope\. #consequence {"status":"current","derives_from":"D-007","handoff":"target"}

[C-020]: Workspace colours should come from the design system\. #constraint {"status":"proposed","derives_from":"D-007"}

[I-014]: What visual treatment marks the current workspace? #issue #mvp {"status":"deferred","parent":"I-010","blocking":false,"nonblocking_reason":"Visual styling can follow later.","defer_reason":"Waiting for the design system."}

[P-014A]: A coloured badge using \-\-color\-\* tokens\, named \<domain\>\_\<verb\>\_\<object\>\, see \`badge\_color\`\. #position {"status":"proposed","issue":"I-014"}

[P-014B]: A plain text label\. #position {"status":"rejected","issue":"I-014"}

[I-020]: How is access assigned today? #issue {"status":"resolved","parent":"I-001","resolved_by":"E-030","resolution_history":["E-030"]}

[E-030]: Access follows explicit assignments\; see \`assign\(\)\` and \[x\] the AT&T &amp\; flags\. #evidence {"status":"verified","sources":[{"kind":"code","ref":"src/access.ts","authority":"observed","locator":"assign()","revision":"abc123"}]}

[P-020]: Access might follow roles\. #position {"status":"proposed","issue":"I-020"}

[I-040]: Should workspaces have landing pages? #issue {"status":"dropped","parent":"I-010","reason":"Operations-first navigation removes the need for workspace landing pages."}

[P-040]: One landing page per workspace\. #position {"status":"proposed","issue":"I-040"}

[AS-001]: Most users switch workspace less than five times a day\. #assumption {"status":"unverified","blocking":false,"nonblocking_reason":"It only tunes the switcher.","validation":"Measure with ten users."}

[AS-002]: Users know their workspace names\. #assumption {"status":"validated","blocking":false,"nonblocking_reason":"Confirmed in research.","validation":"Analytics review."}

[AS-003]: Users never work across workspaces\. #assumption {"status":"invalidated","validation":"Interviews."}

[E-050]: Thirty workspaces is the largest current tenant\. #evidence {"status":"verified","sources":[{"kind":"user","ref":"Fixture tenant list","authority":"intent"}]}

<A-004>: A workspace hierarchy repeats navigation for cross\-workspace work\. #argument {"status":"active","issue":"I-010","based_on":["E-021","C-008"]}

<A-017>: The switcher costs one extra click when changing workspace\. #argument {"status":"active","issue":"I-010"}

